{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/uy5iv8","slide":3,"text":"Figure 4 comparison template, not experimental results. Intended row types are damaged false negative, regional effect, added memory effect, and failure; these types are not claims until real cases are found. Change or drop row purposes that are unsupported. All six columns use the same geographic crop and output resolution per row. Keep model checkpoint/protocol consistent with the reported ablation. Use actual GT and predictions, never recolour source-paper reference maps as model outputs. Legend is a proposed consistent palette and must be mapped to the actual class IDs. If magnified insets are added, use identical positions and scales across columns. Qualitative cases do not replace aggregate Damaged precision/recall/F1 and event-level evaluation."}